.TH BS 1 "November 2026" "booker-search 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bs \- fuzzy file finder with SSH support
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bs
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ QUERY ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bs
is a fuzzy file finder with an interactive TUI and SSH support.
When invoked without arguments it opens the interactive interface.
When a
.I QUERY
argument is supplied it runs the search non\-interactively and prints
matching paths to standard output, one per line.
.PP
Search results use the on-disk index by default; live filesystem scans
are added in
.B both
mode (the default).
SSH locations are searched transparently.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I QUERY
Search query to run non\-interactively.
Must be at least 2 characters.
Omit to open the interactive TUI.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-target " <TARGET>"
What to search.
One of:
.B files
(default),
.BR dirs ,
.BR all ,
.BR content .
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " <MODE>"
Search mode.
One of:
.B both
(default),
.BR index ,
.BR live .
\fBindex\fR queries the on-disk database only (fast, may be stale).
\fBlive\fR walks the filesystem / SSH host live (slower, always current).
\fBboth\fR runs index first then live to fill in new files.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-content
Also search inside file contents (grep).
Results are printed as
\fIpath\fR:\fIline\fR:\fItext\fR.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-case\-sensitive
Case\-sensitive matching.
Default is case\-insensitive.
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-consecutive
Consecutive matching: query characters must appear in the filename in
order with no gaps.
Default is standard fuzzy matching (characters may skip positions).
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-location " <LOCATION>"
Restrict results to a single location, matched by name or ID
(case\-insensitive name match).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-limit " <N>"
Maximum number of results to print.
Default is 100.
.TP
.BR \-0 ", " \-\-null
Separate output paths with NUL bytes instead of newlines.
Useful with
.BR xargs (1)
.BR \-0 .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a brief help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version number and exit.
.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
When run without a
.I QUERY
argument,
.B bs
opens a full\-screen interactive TUI.
The index is searched as you type; live searches start after a short debounce.
.SS Navigation
.TP
.BR "Up / Down"
Move cursor through results.
.TP
.BR "PgUp / PgDn"
Jump by one page.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the selected file in the configured editor.
.TP
.B Esc
Clear the query and cancel all running searches.
.SS Search Toggles
.TP
.B ^F
Toggle content search on/off (grep inside file contents).
.TP
.B ^T
Cycle search target: files \(-> dirs \(-> all \(-> content.
Filters in\-place when possible; restarts search only when necessary.
.TP
.B ^S
Cycle search mode: index \(-> live \(-> both.
.TP
.B ^Z
Toggle fuzzy / consecutive matching.
.TP
.B ^A
Toggle case\-sensitive matching.
.TP
.B ^L
Cycle location filter: all \(-> location[0] \(-> location[1] \(-> \&.\|.\|.
Smart behaviour: filters in\-place when the target location has already
finished searching; keeps the target\(aqs task running and cancels others
when it is still in progress; restarts only the target when it has not
been searched yet.
.SS Results
.TP
.B ^N
Show file / directory info popup for the selected result.
.TP
.B "^C  /  Right"
Open the file browser at the selected result.
.SS Index
.TP
.B ^R
Rebuild the search index from all configured locations.
.SS Status / Controls Bars
.TP
.B ^V
Expand / collapse the status bar.
.TP
.B ^H
Show / hide the status bar.
.TP
.B ^K
Show / hide the controls bar.
.SS Application
.TP
.B Tab
Open the settings / menu popup.
.TP
.B ^Q
Quit.
.SS Settings Popup
.TP
.BR "Left / Right"
Switch tab (Settings \(bu Locations \(bu Keys \(bu Manual).
.TP
.BR "Up / Down"
Navigate items / scroll the manual.
.TP
.BR "Enter / Space"
Toggle a setting or activate an item.
.TP
.BR "Tab / Esc"
Close the popup.
.SS Locations Tab
.TP
.B a
Add a new location.
.TP
.BR "e / Enter"
Edit the selected location.
.TP
.B d
Delete the selected location.
.TP
.B Space
Toggle location enabled / disabled.
.TP
.B ^Z
Test the SSH connection (in the edit form).
.SH WILDCARD SEARCH
Type
.B *
or
.B ?
anywhere in your query to switch into glob mode.
Wildcards are detected automatically; no mode toggle is needed.
.TP
.B *
Matches any sequence of characters (including none).
.TP
.B ?
Matches exactly one character.
.PP
If the pattern contains no
.BR / ,
it matches against the filename only.
If the pattern contains
.BR / ,
it matches against the full path.
Case sensitivity follows the
.B ^A
setting (interactive) or
.B \-\-case\-sensitive
flag (CLI).
.PP
Examples:
.IP
.nf
\fB*.rs\fR            All Rust source files
\fBtest_*\fR          Files beginning with \(lqtest_\(rq
\fBREADME*\fR         README, README.md, README.txt, etc.
\fBsrc/*/main.rs\fR   main.rs one level deep under src/
\fBsrc/**/*_test.rs\fR  any _test.rs under src/ at any depth
.fi
.PP
Wildcard mode replaces fuzzy/consecutive matching entirely.
The
.B [wildcard]
badge appears in the search bar when active.
Combine with content search
.RB ( \-f " / " ^F )
to grep inside matched files.
.SH SEARCH RESULTS
Results are shown in four columns in the interactive TUI:
.TP
.B Location
The configured location name the file belongs to.
.TP
.B Match
Match type and source:
.RS
.TP
.B "[filename] I"
Filename match from the on\-disk index.
.TP
.B "[filename] S"
Filename match from a live scan.
.TP
.B "[directory] I"
Directory from the index.
.TP
.B "[content] S"
Content (grep) match, always live.
.RE
.TP
.B Path
The file or directory path.
.TP
.B Preview
Content matches show the matching line after a vertical bar.
.SH SETTINGS
.TP
.B Content Search
When on, searches inside file contents in addition to filenames.
Uses grep locally and SSH grep on remote locations.
Slower than name\-only search; best used with a specific query.
.TP
.B Search Target
Determines what types of entries are returned:
.BR files " (default), " dirs ", " all ", " content .
.TP
.B Fuzzy / Consecutive Matching
When in consecutive mode, query letters must appear in sequence with no gaps.
Example: \(lqsrc\(rq matches \(lqsource\(rq but not \(lqsearch\(rq.
When off, standard fuzzy matching is used (letters may skip positions).
Wildcard mode overrides both.
.TP
.B Case Sensitive
When on, \(lqREADME\(rq does not match \(lqreadme\(rq.
.TP
.B Editor
Selects which editor opens when you press Enter on a result.
Supported: \fBnvim\fR (default), \fBnano\fR.
.TP
.B Require Unlock on Startup
When on, SSH passwords are stored encrypted (AES\-256\-GCM) and require a
master password each time the application starts.
When off, SSH passwords are stored in a plain JSON file (permissions 600).
.PP
In CLI mode, only plain\-storage credentials and SSH agent authentication
are available; there is no prompt for a master password.
.SH LOCATIONS
Each location is a directory that
.B bs
indexes and searches.
Local locations are walked on disk.
SSH locations connect over SSH.
.PP
Disable a location (Space in the Locations tab) to exclude it from results
without deleting its configuration.
After adding or editing a location, press
.B ^R
to rebuild the index.
.PP
SSH authentication is attempted in this order:
.IP "1." 4
SSH agent (uses an existing loaded key).
.IP "2."
Password authentication.
.IP "3."
Keyboard\-interactive authentication.
.PP
Use
.B ^Z
in the location edit form to test a connection before saving.
SSH host keys are verified using trust\-on\-first\-use (TOFU) and stored in
.IR ~/.config/booker\-search/known_hosts .
A host\-key mismatch aborts the connection with a warning.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/booker\-search/config.toml
Main configuration file (locations, settings).
.TP
.I ~/.config/booker\-search/bs.db
SQLite database used as the search index.
.TP
.I ~/.config/booker\-search/credentials.json
SSH passwords in plain text (permissions 600).
Used when
.B Require Unlock on Startup
is off.
.TP
.I ~/.config/booker\-search/credentials.enc
SSH passwords encrypted with AES\-256\-GCM and an Argon2\-derived key.
Used when
.B Require Unlock on Startup
is on.
.TP
.I ~/.config/booker\-search/known_hosts
SSH host keys accepted by
.B bs
(OpenSSH format, permissions 600).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Open the interactive TUI:
.IP
.B bs
.PP
Find all Rust source files:
.IP
.B "bs '*.rs'"
.PP
Find files matching \(lqmain\(rq with a live scan:
.IP
.B "bs \-m live main"
.PP
Search file contents for \(lqTODO\(rq:
.IP
.B "bs \-f TODO"
.PP
Case\-sensitive search for \(lqConfig\(rq in directories only:
.IP
.B "bs \-c \-t dirs Config"
.PP
Search only the \(lqwork\(rq location and pipe to fzf:
.IP
.B "bs \-l work query | fzf"
.PP
Feed results to xargs (NUL\-separated):
.IP
.B "bs \-0 '*.toml' | xargs \-0 grep \-l dependencies"
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR find (1),
.BR grep (1),
.BR fzf (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh\-add (1)
